            blackBoxWarning = "MALIGNANT HYPERTHERMIA (MH): Potent trigger of malignant hyperthermia in genetically susceptible individuals (mutations in RYR1 or CACNA1S genes). Clinical signs include hypercapnia (rising EtCO2), muscle rigidity, tachycardia, tachypnea, cyanosis, and profound hyperthermia. Stop volatile anesthetic immediately, hyperventilate with 100% O2, and administer IV Dantrolene (2.5 mg/kg stat). PEDIATRIC EMERGENCE AGITATION: Rapid emergence from sevoflurane in children is frequently associated with transient agitation, delirium, and crying (mitigated by fentanyl, dexmedetomidine, or propofol transition).",
