            doses = "Minimum Alveolar Concentration (MAC in 100% O2):\n• Adults (40y): 2.05% (reduces with age: ~1.5% at 70y; MAC in 65% N2O: 1.1%).\n• Neonates / Infants: 3.2% (highest MAC requirement in infants <6 months).\n• Children (1-12y): 2.5%.\n\nInhalation Mask Induction:\n• Incremental Technique: Start at 0.5% in 100% O2 or O2/N2O mixture and increase by 0.5-1% every few breaths up to 5% to 8% until surgical anesthesia achieved.\n• Vital Capacity Rapid Induction: Prime anesthesia circuit with 8% Sevoflurane; patient exhales to residual volume and takes a single maximal vital capacity breath and holds (induces unconsciousness in ~60-90 seconds).\n\nMaintenance of General Anesthesia:\n• 0.5% to 3.0% Sevoflurane with or without Nitrous Oxide.",
