            pkPd = "Fluorinated methyl isopropyl ether. Low blood:gas partition coefficient (0.65), resulting in rapid uptake, rapid alveolar-to-brain equilibration, and rapid elimination/washout upon discontinuation. Non-pungent, sweet, non-irritating odor to the respiratory tract (does not induce coughing, salivation, or breath-holding). Brain:blood partition coefficient 1.7. Undergoes modest hepatic metabolism (~2-5%) by CYP2E1 to hexafluoroisopropanol (HFIP) and inorganic fluoride (F-); HFIP is rapidly glucuronidated and excreted in urine; peak inorganic fluoride levels rarely cause nephrotoxicity (unlike methoxyflurane). Over 95% excreted unchanged by exhalation through lungs.",
