            specialInstructions = "PSEUDOCHOLINESTERASE DEFICIENCY (Prolonged Apnea): Patients with genetic variants of butyrylcholinesterase (atypical dibucaine number) or acquired deficiency (liver disease, pregnancy, malnutrition, organophosphate poisoning) will experience prolonged neuromuscular paralysis and apnea lasting 2 to 6 hours. DO NOT administer reversal agents; continue mechanical ventilation and sedation until spontaneous recovery occurs.",
            pkPd = "Bis-quaternary ammonium compound composed of two joined acetylcholine molecules. Ultra-rapid onset (30-60 seconds, fastest of all NMBAs). Duration of action 5-10 minutes. Extremely rapid hydrolysis in plasma and liver by Butyrylcholinesterase (Pseudocholinesterase / Plasma Cholinesterase) first to Succinylmonocholine (very weak neuromuscular blocker) and then to succinic acid and choline. Less than 10% excreted unchanged in urine. Elimination half-life ~47 seconds.",
