            doses = "MAXIMUM SINGLE SAFE DOSES (CRITICAL SAFETY LIMITS):\n• Plain Lidocaine (without Adrenaline):\n  Adult: 3.0 to 4.5 mg/kg IV/infiltration (ABSOLUTE MAXIMUM SINGLE DOSE: 300 mg = 30 mL of 1% or 15 mL of 2%).\n• Lidocaine with Adrenaline (1:200,000 = 5 mcg/mL Adrenaline):\n  Adult: 7.0 mg/kg infiltration (ABSOLUTE MAXIMUM SINGLE DOSE: 500 mg = 50 mL of 1% with adrenaline).\n  (Adrenaline causes local vasoconstriction, slowing systemic absorption and extending duration of anesthesia by 50-100%).\n• Pediatric: 3.0 to 4.0 mg/kg Plain (max 7 mg/kg with Adrenaline).\n\nBlunting Hemodynamic Response to Intubation:\n• 1.0 to 1.5 mg/kg IV push administered 90 seconds prior to laryngoscopy.\n\nPrevention of Propofol Injection Pain:\n• 0.5 mg/kg IV (or 20 to 40 mg IV) mixed directly with propofol or given into vein with brief proximal tourniquet occlusion.\n\nCardiac Arrest / Pulseless VT/VF (ACLS Protocol):\n• Initial: 1.0 to 1.5 mg/kg IV push; repeat 0.5 to 0.75 mg/kg in 5-10 min (max 3 mg/kg total), then maintenance infusion 1 to 4 mg/min (20 to 50 mcg/kg/min).",
