            blackBoxWarning = "HEPATOTOXICITY WITH CHRONIC ORAL USE: Symptomatic hepatitis and fatal hepatic injury reported with prolonged oral use for chronic spasticity. Periodic LFT monitoring mandatory for oral therapy. (NOTE: Acute IV use for Malignant Hyperthermia has no absolute contraindications because MH is 100% fatal without dantrolene).",
            indications = "SPECIFIC LIFE-SAVING ANTIDOTE FOR MALIGNANT HYPERTHERMIA (MH) crisis triggered by volatile anesthetics (Sevoflurane, Isoflurane, Desflurane) or Succinylcholine; Treatment of Neuroleptic Malignant Syndrome (NMS); Severe Exertional Heat Stroke with rhabdomyolysis.",
            doses = "MALIGNANT HYPERTHERMIA EMERGENCY RESUSCITATION (MHAUS PROTOCOL):\n• Initial Rapid IV Bolus: 2.5 mg/kg IV push IMMEDIATELY upon clinical suspicion (rising EtCO2, masseter spasm, tachycardia, hyperthermia).\n• Repeat Dosing: If clinical and physiological signs (hypercapnia, rigidity, tachycardia) persist, repeat boluses of 1.0 to 2.5 mg/kg IV every 5 to 10 minutes.\n• Maximum Cumulative Dose: Up to 10 mg/kg (some refractory cases may require up to 20-30 mg/kg).\n• Post-Crisis Maintenance: 1.0 mg/kg IV every 4 to 6 hours (or continuous IV infusion 0.25 mg/kg/hour) for AT LEAST 24 to 48 HOURS to prevent recrudescence/relapse of MH (recrudescence occurs in up to 25% of cases within 24 hours).",
            administration = "Administer by rapid intravenous push via large-bore peripheral line or central venous line. RECONSTITUTION INSTRUCTIONS (CRITICAL SPEED): Each 20 mg vial must be reconstituted with 60 mL of sterile water for injection WITHOUT PRESERVATIVES. Shake vigorously until the orange-yellow solution is completely clear (takes 1-3 minutes). A 70 kg adult requiring 2.5 mg/kg needs ~175 mg = approx. 9 VIALS for the initial bolus alone! Modern formulation (Ryanodex): 250 mg lyophilized powder reconstituted in just 5 mL sterile water in <1 minute.",
            timing = "Hospital Operating Room / ICU emergency IV administration only (आपतकालीन रूपमा नसाबाट मात्र दिने).",
            specialInstructions = "MHAUS EMERGENCY ACTIONS: 1) Call for help & MH Cart; 2) Immediately STOP volatile anesthetics and succinylcholine; 3) Hyperventilate with 100% O2 at maximum fresh gas flows (≥10 L/min); 4) Reconstitute and inject Dantrolene 2.5 mg/kg stat; 5) Active cooling (cold IV saline, ice packs to axillae/groin, gastric lavage); 6) Treat hyperkalemia (Calcium chloride/gluconate, Insulin 10 units + 50 mL D50W, Sodium bicarbonate); 7) STRICT CONTRAINDICATION: NEVER administer Calcium Channel Blockers (Verapamil, Diltiazem) with Dantrolene (precipitates fatal myocardial collapse and hyperkalemic arrest).",
            pkPd = "Hydantoin derivative. High lipid solubility. Protein binding ~90%. Reversibly binds to ryanodine receptor-1 (RyR1) channels on the sarcoplasmic reticulum membrane in skeletal muscle, blocking calcium ion release into the sarcoplasm, uncoupling excitation-contraction, and halting the hypermetabolic crisis. Metabolized by hepatic microsomal enzymes by oxidation and reduction to 5-hydroxydantrolene (active) and acetylamino-dantrolene. Excreted renally (25%) and in feces. Elimination half-life ~4-9 hours.",
            renalAdj = "No dosage adjustment in acute MH emergency; each 20 mg vial contains 3 g mannitol (promotes diuresis to protect kidneys from myoglobinuria).",
            hepaticAdj = "No contraindication in acute life-threatening Malignant Hyperthermia.",
