            blackBoxWarning = "DEATH IN PRETERM INFANTS WITH RAPID INFUSION: Deaths reported in preterm infants following rapid intravenous infusion of lipid emulsions due to pulmonary lipid accumulation. (NOTE: In Local Anesthetic Systemic Toxicity [LAST], rapid bolus is life-saving).",
            indications = "FIRST-LINE RESCUE RESUSCITATION PROTOCOL FOR LOCAL ANESTHETIC SYSTEMIC TOXICITY (LAST) induced by bupivacaine, ropivacaine, lidocaine, or other local anesthetics (ASRA 2024 / AAGBI Guidelines); Overdose of other lipophilic cardiac medications (calcium channel blockers, beta-blockers, tricyclic antidepressants, bupropion); Parenteral nutrition source of essential fatty acids.",
            doses = "LOCAL ANESTHETIC SYSTEMIC TOXICITY (LAST RESUSCITATION PROTOCOL - ASRA 2024):\n• Initial Rapid IV Bolus: 1.5 mL/kg of 20% Lipid Emulsion IV push over 1 minute (approx. 100 mL for a 70 kg adult).\n• Immediate Continuous Infusion: 0.25 mL/kg/min IV (approx. 18 mL/min = ~1000 mL/hr for a 70 kg adult).\n• If Hemodynamic Instability Persists:\n  - Repeat the 1.5 mL/kg IV bolus every 3 to 5 minutes (up to 2 additional boluses, total 3 boluses).\n  - Double the continuous infusion rate to 0.5 mL/kg/min.\n• Maximum Recommended Cumulative Dose: 12 mL/kg over the first 60 minutes.\n• Continue infusion for at least 10 to 15 minutes after hemodynamic stability and sinus rhythm are fully restored.",
            administration = "Administer intravenously only. Use dedicated large-bore peripheral or central IV line. Emulsion must be completely homogenous and milk-white; do not use if phase separation has occurred.",
            timing = "Hospital Operating Room / ICU emergency IV administration only (आपतकालीन अवस्थामा मात्र नसाबाट दिने).",
            specialInstructions = "MODIFIED ACLS IN LAST: 1) Stop local anesthetic immediately; 2) Maintain airway with 100% O2 (prevent hypoxia and acidosis which drastically worsen LAST); 3) Treat seizures with Benzodiazepines (Midazolam 1-2 mg IV; avoid large doses of propofol which depress myocardium); 4) CPR with REDUCED ADRENALINE DOSES: Give small doses (<1 mcg/kg, e.g. 10-50 mcg boluses) instead of standard 1 mg ACLS doses (high-dose adrenaline impairs lipid emulsion resuscitation and worsens arrhythmias); 5) AVOID Vasopressin, Calcium Channel Blockers, Beta-blockers, and Lidocaine.",
            pkPd = "Sterile emulsion consisting of 20% soybean oil, 1.2% egg yolk phospholipids, 2.25% glycerin, and water for injection. Acts by multiple mechanisms: 1) 'Lipid Sink / Lipid Sponge' effect: Creates an expanded intravascular lipid phase that sequesters highly lipophilic local anesthetic molecules (bupivacaine partition coefficient 28) away from cardiac sodium channels and brain tissues; 2) Metabolic activation: Overcomes local-anesthetic-induced inhibition of mitochondrial carnitine-acyltransferase and fatty acid beta-oxidation, providing immediate energetic substrate to the ischemic myocardium; 3) Membrane ion channel activation and calcium entry stimulation. Cleared from bloodstream via lipoprotein lipase mimicking chylomicron metabolism. Half-life ~30 minutes.",
            renalAdj = "No dosage adjustment in emergency LAST resuscitation.",
            hepaticAdj = "No dosage adjustment in emergency LAST resuscitation.",
            pregnancy = "Category C. Safe and life-saving in maternal LAST crisis during labor epidural or cesarean section.",
            lactation = "Safe in emergency resuscitation.",
            sideEffects = "Hypertriglyceridemia, pancreatitis (rare, with prolonged excessive infusions), fat overload syndrome, transient interference with laboratory blood tests (lipemic blood interferes with spectrophotometric hemoglobin, electrolyte, and coagulation assays).",
            priceNpr = "NPR 1,200.00 - 2,200.00 per 250mL / 500mL bottle (20% emulsion)",
            priceInr = "INR 750.00 - 1,400.00 per bottle",
            brandsNepal = listOf(
                BrandInfo("Intralipid-Quest", "Quest Pharmaceuticals", "Emulsion for Inj", "20% (250 mL / 500 mL)"),
                BrandInfo("Lipiven-NPL", "Nepal Pharmaceuticals Lab", "Emulsion for Inj", "20% (250 mL)")
            ),
            brandsIndia = listOf(
