            contraindications = "Known hypersensitivity to glycopyrrolate; narrow-angle glaucoma; obstructive uropathy (bladder neck obstruction due to prostatic hypertrophy); obstructive disease of the GI tract (pyloroduodenal stenosis, paralytic ileus); severe ulcerative colitis / toxic megacolon; myasthenia gravis (unless used to treat cholinergic crisis).",
            modeOfAction = "Competitively antagonizes acetylcholine at muscarinic M1, M2, and M3 receptors, selectively blocking parasympathetic neuro-effector junctions in exocrine glands (salivary, bronchial, gastric) and cardiac sinoatrial node, thereby inhibiting secretions, preventing vagal bradycardia, and relaxing smooth muscle.",
