            specialInstructions = "GREATER SENSORY-MOTOR SEPARATION: Pure S-(-)-enantiomer design gives ropivacaine lower lipid solubility than bupivacaine, resulting in significantly less motor blockade at low concentrations (0.1-0.2%). This allows the parturient to walk ('walking epidural') and facilitates early post-op ambulation while preserving profound sensory analgesia.",
